{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm","cve_id":"CVE-2026-87018","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm","summary":"undici vulnerable to Denial of Service via TLS 1.2 certificate-changing renegotiation","description":"## Impact\n\nundici crashes the client process when a TLS 1.2 server renegotiates after the connection is established and presents a different, CA-trusted certificate whose hostname does not match the requested host. Node.js re-runs hostname verification on the renegotiated handshake and destroys the socket with `ERR_TLS_CERT_ALTNAME_INVALID`. undici's established socket error handler asserted that this error code could never occur, so the peer-controlled error became an uncaught `AssertionError` that terminates the Node.js process. Both the HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 paths are affected.\n\nA malicious or compromised HTTPS endpoint reached through undici or the global `fetch()` can crash the client with a single server-initiated renegotiation, taking down all in-flight requests and background work in the process. Only TLS 1.2 is affected, because TLS 1.3 does not support renegotiation. Exploitation does not require a CA compromise: the attacker controls the endpoint and can present two ordinary valid certificates, the first matching the requested URL and the second intentionally not matching it.\n\n## Patches\n\nUpgrade to undici 6.29.1, 7.30.1, or 8.12.2.\n\n## Workarounds\n\nRestrict outbound connections to TLS 1.3, for example by setting `connect: { minVersion: 'TLSv1.3', maxVersion: 'TLSv1.3' }` on the client or agent, so that renegotiation cannot occur, when the target endpoints support TLS 1.3.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nodejs/undici/security-advisories/GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm","source_code_location":"https://github.com/nodejs/undici","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-87018","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-87018","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/12cfd96c3f430897656e3edc1c5e02be8c1cd309","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b40fbfc0651703cf9fa9f6ced68b679f28d8bb28","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/e257e9f8fb42eedd50727b9cf65e548c8925e4a8","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v6.29.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v7.30.1","https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v8.12.2","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qrxm-fqhp-jwvm"],"published_at":"2026-10-27T19:02:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-27T19:02:22Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-27T19:02:21Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-10-15T19:17:46Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 4.2.1, < 6.29.1","first_patched_version":"6.29.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 7.0.0, < 7.30.1","first_patched_version":"7.30.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"undici"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 8.0.0, < 8.12.2","first_patched_version":"8.12.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","score":7.5},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-248","name":"Uncaught Exception"},{"cwe_id":"CWE-617","name":"Reachable Assertion"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"benzdeus","id":53105746,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTA1NzQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53105746?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benzdeus","html_url":"https://github.com/benzdeus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benzdeus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benzdeus/following{/oth